00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:26.490
<v Speaker 2>Let's say a goat, right?

317
00:30:26.490 --> 00:30:32.610
<v Speaker 2>You own a goat and so you take care of it, right?

318
00:30:32.610 --> 00:30:33.610
<v Speaker 2>Because it's your property.

319
00:30:33.930 --> 00:30:35.290
<v Speaker 2>But you don't buy gifts.

320
00:30:36.650 --> 00:30:39.370
<v Speaker 2>You're not going to buy your goat jewelry, right?

321
00:30:40.090 --> 00:30:40.490
<v Speaker 2>Why?

322
00:30:41.690 --> 00:30:42.770
<v Speaker 2>Because you don't need to.

323
00:30:42.770 --> 00:30:43.610
<v Speaker 2>It's a goat.

324
00:30:44.450 --> 00:30:45.610
<v Speaker 2>It's part of your property.

325
00:30:45.850 --> 00:30:51.850
<v Speaker 2>So in the old days, slaves were no different than a goat or an animal, right?

326
00:30:52.250 --> 00:30:56.490
