358
00:34:10.010 --> 00:34:10.330
<v Speaker 2>Right?

359
00:34:10.410 --> 00:34:16.730
<v Speaker 2>The word na'een is the superlative form of na'am or ni'am and it means the greatest gift of all.

360
00:34:18.130 --> 00:34:21.210
<v Speaker 2>What is that greatest gift of all that has been given to us?

361
00:34:21.610 --> 00:34:22.730
<v Speaker 2>Iman, faith.

362
00:34:23.770 --> 00:34:25.130
<v Speaker 2>That is the ultimate gift.

363
00:34:25.690 --> 00:34:31.050
<v Speaker 2>On the day of judgment, Allah will ask us about our iman which is the greatest blessing of all.

364
00:34:31.330 --> 00:34:35.770
<v Speaker 2>Otherwise, what was the purpose of giving us all these gifts and making us different from animals?

365
00:34:38.730 --> 00:34:38.930
<v Speaker 2>Right?

366
00:34:38.970 --> 00:34:44.330
<v Speaker 2>If I give you a gift, I expect you to use it for the purpose that I gave it to you for.

367
00:34:44.970 --> 00:34:50.050
<v Speaker 2>So, if that was not the case, animals have eyes, animals have ears, right?

368
00:34:50.250 --> 00:34:51.930
<v Speaker 2>But they don't have the intellect that we have.

369
00:34:52.490 --> 00:34:53.450
<v Speaker 2>They don't have iman.

370
00:34:55.330 --> 00:35:03.530
<v Speaker 2>So the idea of all these gifts and intellect most of all is so that we can develop iman.

371
00:35:04.810 --> 00:35:06.570
<v Speaker 2>So that we can become different from animals.

372
00:35:06.570 --> 00:35:12.810
<v Speaker 2>So that we can see creation, reflect upon it and then recognize him and try to get closer to him.

373
00:35:13.690 --> 00:35:14.330
<v Speaker 2>You understand?

374
00:35:17.210 --> 00:35:23.050
<v Speaker 2>So now we're learning that Allah as Rab is someone who not only owns us

